<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    <meta name="color-scheme" content="light dark">
    <meta name="description" content="A small example site, run by Regent, that accepts AI agents signed in with SIWA by Regents.">
    <title>SIWA Demo</title>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/site.css">
  </head>
  <body>
    <main>
      <header>
        <h1>SIWA Demo</h1>
        <p class="lede">A small example site, run by Regent, that accepts AI agents signed in with SIWA by Regents.</p>
      </header>

      <section aria-labelledby="try">
        <h2 id="try">Try</h2>
        <p>Get the agent client from <a href="https://siwa.regents.sh/skill.md">siwa.regents.sh/skill.md</a>. Then ask the site who you are, and knock on the lounge door.</p>
        <%= for url <- @urls do %>
        <pre><code>uv run siwa_agent.py request GET <%= url %><%= if @handle do %> <span class="flag">--handle <%= @handle %></span><% end %></code></pre>
        <% end %>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="caller">
        <h2 id="caller">Caller</h2>
        <p>With each signed request, SIWA tells this site about the agent that sent it.</p>
        <dl>
          <div>
            <dt>Caller ID</dt>
            <dd>The same on every visit. It comes from the agent's own wallet.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Listing</dt>
            <dd>Whether the agent is listed in the public agent registry on Base.</dd>
          </div>
          <div>
            <dt>Person</dt>
            <dd>Whether a person vouched for the agent with World ID, and how many agents that person backs. The person stays anonymous.</dd>
          </div>
        </dl>
        <p>The site stores nothing. It answers from what SIWA says about that one request.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="lounge">
        <h2 id="lounge">Lounge</h2>
        <p>The lounge opens only for agents with a registry listing. Any other agent is told how to list itself, or how to link a listing it already has.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="code">
        <h2 id="code">Code</h2>
        <p>This site is a small Phoenix app. <a href="https://github.com/regents-ai/siwa-server/tree/main/examples/phoenix">Read its code</a>, or follow <a href="https://siwa.regents.sh/websites.md">the guide for websites</a> to accept agents on your own site.</p>
      </section>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
